::ENG2_U05_L04_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.V.03] Sentence: "During the science demonstration, students had to _____ how the liquid changed color." Which word is most precise?{
=A. observe#Correct. Observe means watch carefully to learn or understand, which fits the science context.
~B. ignore#Incorrect. Ignore has the opposite meaning.
~C. forget#Incorrect. Forget does not fit the task.
~D. decorate#Incorrect. Decorate is unrelated.
}

::ENG2_U05_L04_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.V.03] Which pair is made of antonyms?{
~A. precise and exact#Incorrect. These are synonyms.
=B. vague and precise#Correct. Vague and precise have opposite meanings.
~C. observe and watch#Incorrect. These are related synonyms.
~D. analyze and examine#Incorrect. These are related synonyms.
}

::ENG2_U05_L04_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Dictionary entry: Analyze means to examine carefully by separating into parts. Which paraphrase is accurate for "Students will analyze the paragraph's structure"?{
~A. Students will ignore the paragraph.#Incorrect. Analyze does not mean ignore.
~B. Students will copy the paragraph without thinking.#Incorrect. Analyze requires careful examination.
=C. Students will examine the paragraph's parts carefully.#Correct. This paraphrase uses the dictionary meaning accurately.
~D. Students will decorate the paragraph.#Incorrect. This is unrelated.
}

::ENG2_U05_L04_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.V.02] Which word family connection can help with the meaning of structure?{
=A. struct means build#Correct. Structure is connected to the idea of something built or arranged.
~B. re means again#Incorrect. Re is not the key part in structure.
~C. pre means before#Incorrect. Pre is not part of structure.
~D. un means not#Incorrect. Un is not part of structure.
}

::ENG2_U05_L04_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.V.03] Why should a writer use context after checking a thesaurus?{
~A. Because every synonym always fits.#Incorrect. Synonyms are not always interchangeable.
~B. Because word meaning does not matter.#Incorrect. Meaning is the reason for using context.
~C. Because reference materials are never useful.#Incorrect. They are useful when used carefully.
=D. Because context determines which related word is most precise.#Correct. Context helps the writer choose the word that actually fits.
}
